{# Regular events — classes, clubs, weekly markets — grouped by day.

   Renders nothing when there are none, so it is safe to leave in place.

   These are fixtures, not events: they never appear in the upcoming list,
   because a weekly class expanded into dated occurrences would bury the
   one-off events the page exists to show. Grouping by day is also how
   people actually think about them ("what's on a Tuesday?").

   Only currently-active regulars appear — see the from/until/except
   fields in events.json. A class that stopped for the summer stops
   showing on its own. #}

{% set byDay = events.regulars | regularsByDay %}
{% if byDay | length %}
<section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="regulars-h">
  <h2 id="regulars-h">Every week in Largs</h2>
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <p class="page-intro">Classes, clubs and groups that meet regularly. Anything
  open to the public in Largs can be listed here, free — see below to add one.</p>

  {% for group in byDay %}
  <div class="regular-day">
    <h3 class="regular-dayname">{{ group.day }}</h3>
    {% for r in group.items %}
    <article class="regular">
      {% if r.time %}<div class="regular-time">{{ r.time }}</div>{% endif %}
      <div class="regular-body">
        <h4 class="regular-title">{{ r.title }}</h4>
        {% if r.venue %}<p class="regular-meta">{{ r.venue }}</p>{% endif %}
        {% if r.blurb %}<p class="regular-blurb">{{ r.blurb }}</p>{% endif %}
        {% if r.contact %}<p class="regular-contact">{{ r.contact }}</p>{% endif %}
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</section>
{% endif %}
